<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kech District</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kech is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, centred on the Kech valley and the town of Turbat. Its date-palm oases made it the heart of Makran, ruled in the 19th century by the Gichki family as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the Khanate of Kalat. The valley also holds the ancient settlement mound of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miri">Miri</a> Qalat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kech-district.jpg" alt="Kech District" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hussain Masoom · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meri_A_Kalat.02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
